    {
      "id": "GENUS_ANADENUS",
      "name": "Anadenus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Anadenus — a genus of gastropodas.",
      "lineage": "Anadenus",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_ALTIVAGUS",
          "name": "Anadenus altivagus",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Pale gray-orange preserved, probably red-orange alive; usually unicolor but sometimes with black blotches (Wiktor 2001). </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Club-shaped penis (broadened toward its base), with narrow epiphallus on its apex; hooked, hardened spines or bristles inside lower part of penis, and a single papilla inside its apex; massive spermatheca 2x penis length and with short, thick duct (Wiktor 2001).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Juveniles: Sometimes have lateral bands (Wiktor 2001).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Size: To 75 mm long preserved, mantle length to 43 mm, body width 24 mm; alive and extended, may be to 200 mm long, 40 mm wide (Wiktor 2001).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9775005",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "7f3c34fb-8482-503-a90-7718d548b904d6",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
