        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_BLANFORDI_GODWIN_AUSTEN_1882",
          "name": "Anadenus blanfordi Godwin-Austen, 1882",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Preserved: dark yellow-brown, with some dark marks on the top of the dorsum; strongly diamond-shaped tubercles on skin (Wiktor 2001). </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Short epiphallus; cylindrical penis, slightly narrowed in the middle, and with a small protuberance on one side of the apex; papilla inside the penis apex, and internal ridges along its length (Wiktor 2001)</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Genitalia resemble those of <em>A. yantzeensis</em> (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9708750",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "8f529ff4-2cbe-596-aef-54f3bbf9604a4c",
          "sourceIds": {
