        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_GONGGASHANENSIS_WIKTOR_D_N_CHEN_M_WU_2000",
          "name": "Anadenus gonggashanensis Wiktor, D.-N.Chen & M.Wu, 2000",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Pale spot in the middle of the mantle (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Long vas deferens; long, coiled epiphallus that is encircled by penial retractor at punction with penis; penis narrow, widened at both ends, and rounded sac connected to anterior side of penis; papilla with tubercles inside the posterior end of the penis and long folds in the rest of the penis and attached sac; very large spermatheca, much longer than duct and equal to length of penis; spermatheca duct connects to oviduct; very short atrium; spermatheca 100 mm long with flagellum at one end (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Unique characters of <em>A. gonggashanensis </em>among <em>Anadenus</em> species are the rounded sac attached to penis and the narrowness of penis (Wiktor 2001).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9711538",
          "authorship": "Wiktor, D.-N.Chen & M.Wu",
          "yearPublished": "2000",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "96fcb9da-978d-595-830-246d594d93ebfa"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_NEPALENSIS_WIKTOR_2001",
          "name": "Anadenus nepalensis Wiktor, 2001",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Light brown-cream, olive, or brown alive, sometimes with brown or black lateral streaks, chevron-patterns along the dorsum, or black spots; some have orange spot on mantle and two orange lateral stripes on tail; darker neck and mantle; pale orange-cream sole; thick-set body; low, fine wrinkles relative to its genus, with longitudinal lines separating blocks of tubercles (Wiktor 2001). </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Internal shell 10 x 7 mm; club shaped penis broadened toward base; inside penis, a large, tongue-shaped, ridged ligula that has a digital process toward the penis's base; short epiphallus; spermatheca the length of the penis with short, relatively narrow duct (Wiktor 2001).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Genitalia similar to those of <em>A. yangtzeensis</em> and <em>A. altivagus</em> (Wiktor 2001).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Juveniles: More well-defined patterns and darker than adults (Wiktor 2001).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9795079",
          "authorship": "Wiktor",
          "yearPublished": "2001",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "a9f998b9-24d6-5ff-b46-9248b59661ccb3",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "DCQH"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:DCQH"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_PARVIPENIS_WIKTOR_DE_NIU_MING_2000",
          "name": "Anadenus parvipenis Wiktor, De-Niu & Ming, 2000",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Olive brown body and sole on preserved animals, with black lateral marks on mantle and sides below mantle, and tiny black spots over entire body and sole (Wiktor et al. 2000). </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Penis conical and small, with tongue-shaped internal ligula; spermatheca 2x length of penis, long, and club-shaped, with spherical duct 1/2 its length; epiphallus 12x length of penis and thick; thick oviduct (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Unique characters of <em>A. parvipenis</em> among <em>Anadenus</em> species are small penis, very long and thick epiphallus, thin penial retractor muscle (Wiktor 2001).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9658982",
          "authorship": "Wiktor, De-Niu & Ming",
          "yearPublished": "2000",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "e4721c2a-cf83-5c0-b74-568d426015a263"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_YANGTZEENSIS_WIKTOR_DE_NIU_MING_2000",
          "name": "Anadenus yangtzeensis Wiktor, De-Niu & Ming, 2000",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Preserved: reddish brown body and sole, sometimes with 0.5 mm diam black spots throughout and/or black marks on mantle and lateral stripe of black spots (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Penis expanding towards base, with small bent appendix on its apex, and large wrinkled ligula inside its base; short appendix on penis apex; spermatheca narrow and about as long as penis; epiphallus and vas deferens thin; genitalia similar to those of <em>A. blanfordi </em>(Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Unique characters of <em>A. yangtzeensis</em> among <em>Anadenus</em> species are little black spots on body, relatively thin vas deferens and epiphallus, appendix on penis, large ligula in penis (Wiktor 2001).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9740163",
          "authorship": "Wiktor, De-Niu & Ming",
          "yearPublished": "2000",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "487a023b-8a4b-5ed-8c3-8cdd721ab08aa6"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ANADENUS_YUNNANENSIS_WIKTOR_DE_NIU_MING_2000",
          "name": "Anadenus yunnanensis Wiktor, De-Niu & Ming, 2000",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Anadenus",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Preserved: black body; strong, big wrinkles on dorsum with a triangular cross-section (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Relatively small genitalia; epiphallus joins on side apex of penis (Wiktor 2001); short epiphallus and vas deferens; short, thin oviduct; wide penial retractor; spermatheca with thick, cylindrical duct (Wiktor et al. 2000).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Unique characters of <em>A. yunnanensis</em> among <em>Anadenus</em> are very wide, triangular-in-cross-section wrinkles and short vas deferens (Wiktor 2001).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9762738",
          "authorship": "Wiktor, De-Niu & Ming",
          "yearPublished": "2000",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "cfaafa33-c139-5fe-bad-e506c43df955f2"
        },
